# Intel AX200 Bluetooth (8087:0029) - never let the radio USB-runtime-suspend.
#
# Why: on this t14 (AMD Renoir/Cezanne) the radio hangs off xhci_hcd 0000:06:00.4
# as usb 4-4. When it is runtime-suspended it can come back wedged: it refuses
# re-addressing ("device not accepting address N, error -62"), a port power cycle
# does not revive it, and the kernel's failed cleanup takes the whole xHCI
# controller down ("HC died"). That kills Bluetooth *and* the fingerprint reader
# on 4-3, and only a full poweroff brings the radio back - a PCI remove/rescan of
# 06:00.4 revives the controller but the radio re-wedges and kills it again.
#
# Observed twice: 2026-08-07 09:38 (recovered as hci1) and 2026-08-08 00:23 (did not).
#
# Numbered above systemd's 60-autosuspend.rules so this wins.
# The real enforcement is modprobe.d/btusb-no-autosuspend.conf - btusb re-enables
# autosuspend during probe, which runs after this rule. This is belt-and-braces.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="8087", ATTR{idProduct}=="0029", \
    TEST=="power/control", ATTR{power/control}="on"
